.\" gwt - read-only terminal inspector for git worktrees
.TH GWT 1 "2026-09-16" "gwt 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gwt \- read\-only terminal inspector for git worktrees across multiple repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gwt
.RI [ options ]
.I REPO_PATH
.RI [ REPO_PATH .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gwt
lists every worktree of one or more git repositories and reports, per worktree:
the real repository name, the worktree path, the checked\-out branch, the number of
modified tracked files, the number of untracked files, the configured upstream, and
an ahead/behind count computed from local refs only.
.PP
A path may be a main worktree, any subdirectory of a repository, or any linked
worktree; it is resolved to the repository that contains it, following normal git
semantics.
.PP
.B gwt
is strictly read\-only. It never runs
.BR fetch ,
.BR pull ,
.BR checkout ,
.BR reset ,
.BR clean ,
.BR prune ,
.BR gc ,
.BR add ,
.BR commit ,
.BR rm ,
.BR mv ,
or any
.B worktree
subcommand that mutates state. Every git invocation is made with
.B \-\-no\-optional\-locks
and
.BR GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0 ,
so even the index refresh that
.B git status
would normally write back is suppressed. No network access is performed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON instead of the table. Field names and null semantics are stable; see the
JSON section below.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N"
Force the table width instead of detecting the terminal width.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-truncate
Do not truncate columns to fit the terminal. Useful when redirecting to a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-untracked " all|normal"
How untracked files are counted. With
.B all
(the default) each file inside an untracked directory is counted; with
.B normal
an entire untracked directory counts as one entry.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Colour policy. The default
.B auto
enables colour only when stdout is a real terminal.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SEC"
Per\-invocation git timeout in seconds. The default is 120;
.B 0
disables the timeout.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit with status 1 when any worktree needs attention, instead of only when an input
path fails to resolve.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH "TABLE COLUMNS"
.TP
.B 仓库 (repository)
Real repository name; the main worktree is marked
.BR [main] .
.TP
.B worktree path
Full path. When space is tight it is truncated from the left so the tail stays
recognisable.
.TP
.B branch
The branch name, or
.BR "(detached) <sha>" ,
.BR "(unborn) <branch>" ,
.BR "(bare)" ,
or
.B "(unknown HEAD)" .
.TP
.B modified
Count of modified tracked files, including staged, unstaged and conflicted entries;
a rename or copy counts once. Shown as
.B \-
when the path is gone \- never as 0.
.TP
.B untracked
Count of untracked files, excluding ignored ones.
.TP
.B upstream
The upstream ref name;
.B "(none)"
when no upstream is configured;
.B "<name> (ref missing locally)"
when one is configured but the local ref does not exist;
.B \-
when not applicable.
.TP
.B ahead/behind
Written as
.BR +ahead/\-behind ,
for example
.BR +1/\-2 .
.B \-
means not applicable;
.B ?
means the value cannot be computed.
.SH "JSON OUTPUT"
The document contains
.BR schema ,
.BR tool ,
.BR version ,
.BR generated_at ,
.BR read_only ,
.BR fetched ,
.BR untracked_mode ,
.BR notes ,
.BR summary ,
.B repos
and
.BR errors .
Each worktree reports
.BR head.state
(one of
.BR branch ,
.BR detached ,
.BR unborn ,
.BR unknown ),
.BR tracked_modified ,
.BR untracked ,
.BR conflicts ,
and an
.B upstream
object whose
.B state
distinguishes
.B none
(no upstream configured) from
.B missing_ref
(configured but the local ref is absent).
.PP
Unknown values are reported as
.B null
or
.BR unknown ;
they are never silently reported as zero.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
All input paths resolved. Worktree\-level problems do not fail the run unless
.B \-\-strict
is given.
.TP
.B 1
An input path could not be resolved, or
.B \-\-strict
was given and some worktree needs attention.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or git could not be found.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the worktrees of two repositories:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gwt ~/code/alpha ~/code/beta
.EE
.RE
.PP
Inspect the summary as JSON:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gwt \-\-json ~/code/alpha | jq .summary
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fail a script when anything needs attention:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gwt \-\-strict ~/code/alpha
.EE
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
Ahead/behind is derived from local refs only, so it lags the remote until you fetch;
upstream.ref_commit_date shows how old the local ref is.
.PP
Only counts are reported, never file lists; stash entries, submodule internals and
ignored files are not counted.
.PP
Worktrees whose directory has been deleted are reported from registration data only,
and
.B gwt
never prunes them for you.
.PP
This build supports Linux only, because determining whether stdout is a terminal and
querying its width uses Linux ioctls.
.PP
A terminal narrower than 82 columns cannot show all columns; the table then stays at
82 columns rather than squeezing columns below their minimum, and a hint is printed.
.SH AUTHOR
xiangnan0811
.PP
Source: https://github.com/xiangnan0811/gwt
